</div>
</section>

<!-- §04 — DUAL-HEAD VERIFICATION -->
<section id="s-arch" data-code="arch">
<div class="section-no">04 — Architecture</div>
<h2>Dual-head verification in a single forward pass</h2>

<p>The target model already processes the full sequence (context + candidate segment + quality prompt) for quality scoring. SafeSpec attaches a tiny 2-layer MLP safety head that reads the hidden state at the <strong>segment boundary</strong> — the last token of the candidate segment, immediately before the quality-scoring suffix.</p>

<p>This boundary-aligned extraction is crucial: it prevents the scoring prompt tokens from leaking into the safety signal. The MLP sees the model's internal representation of the candidate segment in context — exactly the information needed to predict whether it continues toward harmful content. Since the target model's forward pass happens anyway, extracting this hidden state costs nothing extra.</p>

