<p>SafeSpec achieves the only Pareto-dominant result: 7% ASR (–15 pp vs SecDecoding, –58 pp vs no defense) while maintaining 2.06× speedup on benign workloads. By contrast, SafeDecoding runs at 0.82× — slower than an unaccelerated model — and SecDecoding at 0.61×.</p>

<p>On DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-70B, SafeSpec similarly achieves 7% ASR and 1.76× speedup. The over-refusal rate (XSTest) is 10% — far below SecDecoding's 42% — because the soft recovery mechanism allows false-positive safety alerts to self-correct during multi-sampling rather than terminating the response.</p>

