<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: SafeSpec — Jailbreak Defense Inside the Verify Loop</h2>
    <p>Speculative decoding accelerates LLM inference by having a small draft model propose candidate segments and a large target model verify them — cutting latency by 2× or more. But the verify step has no safety awareness. Existing safety defenses either break the draft-verify mechanism or slow the model below the unaccelerated baseline.</p>
    <p>SafeSpec fixes this by attaching a lightweight 2-layer MLP safety head to the target model's boundary hidden state — computed for free during the verification pass already happening. When the safety head detects a jailbreak, instead of refusing, it rolls back to the previous safe state, inserts a reflection prompt, and samples K candidate continuations, selecting the one with the highest safety score. On Qwen3-32B, this achieves 7% average attack success rate — 15 points better than the best baseline — while maintaining a 2.06× speedup and only 10% over-refusal, versus 42% for the next-best defense.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：SafeSpec——将越狱防御内嵌到验证循环中</h2>
    <p>推测解码通过让小型草稿模型提出候选片段、大型目标模型并行验证，将延迟降低两倍以上。但验证步骤本身没有安全意识。现有安全防御要么破坏草稿-验证机制，要么让模型速度低于无加速基线。</p>
    <p>SafeSpec通过在目标模型的边界隐藏状态上附加一个轻量级两层MLP安全头解决了这个问题——该计算在验证过程中已经发生，完全免费。当安全头检测到越狱时，系统不是拒绝，而是回滚到上一个安全状态，插入反思提示，并对K个候选延续进行采样，选择安全评分最高的那个。在Qwen3-32B上，这将平均攻击成功率降至7%——比最优基线低15个百分点——同时保持2.06倍加速，过度拒绝率仅为10%，而次优防御方法的过度拒绝率高达42%。</p>
  </div>
